			"id":"b99f42a417c922f2",
			"type":"text",
			"text":"01  CONVERSATION BRAINSTORM\nNGHĨ → THẢO LUẬN CẶP → CHIA SẺ  |  Home, freedom, belonging  |  10–12 phút\nStudent: __________________________________  Date: ______________  Partner: ______________________\nTODAY’S OUTCOMES\nDùng 15 collocations; nhận diện paraphrase/distractors trong hai bài nghe; trả lời Speaking Parts 1–3; vận dụng mệnh đề điều kiện và thời gian nói về tương lai.\n\nA. Khởi động – Trả lời trước khi xem bài mẫu\n1.  What makes a place feel like home?\n   Hỏi sâu: Which matters more: familiar people or a familiar environment?\n2.  Would you move abroad for better opportunities?\n   Hỏi sâu: What would you gain, and what might you lose?\n3.  Is it possible to feel lonely in a crowded city?\n   Hỏi sâu: Can you give a personal or hypothetical example?\n4.  When should someone leave their hometown?\n   Hỏi sâu: Is moving away an act of courage, necessity or ambition?\nB. Brainstorm – Ghi từ khóa, chưa cần viết câu hoàn chỉnh\nReasons to STAY\tReasons to MOVE\tWhat I would sacrifice\n\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\n\nC. Speaking challenge – Trình bày quan điểm trong 60 giây\nPosition → Reason → Real or imagined example → Trade-off → Final view\nI would probably ______ because ______. For instance, ______. The downside is ______, but ______.\n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \nMỤC TIÊU  Bảo vệ quan điểm và phản hồi ý kiến khác mà không học thuộc.\n \n02  15 COLLOCATIONS\n10 CỤM MỚI + 5 CỤM ÔN TẬP  |  Hiểu nghĩa → Dùng đúng → Ghi nhớ\n#\tCollocation\tNghĩa tiếng Việt / Example\n01\ta sense of belonging\tcảm giác thuộc về\nMoving away can weaken your sense of belonging.\n02\tput down roots\tổn định, gắn bó lâu dài\nSome graduates hope to put down roots abroad.\n03\tsettle into a new environment\tthích nghi nơi sống mới\nIt takes time to settle into a new environment.\n04\tadjust to local customs\tthích nghi tập quán địa phương\nStudents often adjust to local customs gradually.\n05\tcultural identity\tbản sắc văn hoá\nLanguage is part of our cultural identity.\n06\trelocate for work\tchuyển nơi ở vì công việc\nMany young adults relocate for work.\n07\tbroader career prospects\ttriển vọng nghề nghiệp rộng hơn\nA larger city may offer broader career prospects.\n08\tmake a fresh start\tbắt đầu lại\nMoving abroad can be a chance to make a fresh start.\n09\ta close-knit community\tcộng đồng gắn bó\nI grew up in a close-knit community.\n10\tfeel homesick\tnhớ nhà\nI might feel homesick during the first few months.\n11 R\tquality of life\tchất lượng cuộc sống\nGreen spaces can improve quality of life.\n12 R\tjob opportunities\tcơ hội việc làm\nYoung people look for better job opportunities.\n13 R\tcost of living\tchi phí sinh hoạt\nThe cost of living is high downtown.\n14 R\tsense of community\tsự gắn kết cộng đồng\nShared events build a sense of community.\n15 R\twork-life balance\tcân bằng công việc/cuộc sống\nCommuting can affect work-life balance.\n\nBài vận dụng – Điền từ và nói\n1. After moving to Canada, she found it difficult to ____________________________.\n2. He hopes to ____________________________ in a town where his family feels welcome.\n3. Young graduates sometimes ____________________________ to improve their ____________________________.\nNÓI 30 GIÂY: Dùng 3 cụm từ mới và 1 cụm đã ôn, không gượng ép.\n \n03  PHILOSOPHY LAB\nFREEDOM vs BELONGING  |  Nhiều lựa chọn có đồng nghĩa với hạnh phúc?\nTHE CORE CONFLICT\nTỰ DO là khả năng tự lựa chọn con đường sống. CẢM GIÁC THUỘC VỀ là được chấp nhận và gắn kết với người khác. Rời quê có thể mở rộng cơ hội nhưng làm yếu các quan hệ thân quen; ở lại có thể mang đến an toàn nhưng ít lựa chọn hơn. Không có đáp án đúng tuyệt đối: cần xét hoàn cảnh, giá trị và cái giá phải đánh đổi.\n\nKnowledge / Insight – So sánh hai lập luận đối lập\nPosition A  |  Freedom first\tPosition B  |  Belonging first\nPeople grow when they explore unfamiliar environments.\tStable relationships give life meaning and emotional security.\nA new city may offer education, work and independence.\tA familiar community offers trust, support and identity.\nRisk: choice without connection may create loneliness.\tRisk: security may discourage personal growth.\n\nThí nghiệm tư duy – Một lựa chọn không dễ dàng\nYou receive a scholarship abroad that could transform your career. You would spend five years away from your family, and you do not know anyone in the new country.\n1. Bạn sẽ chọn gì? Giải thích lựa chọn bằng tiếng Anh.\n   \n   \n   \n   \n2. Điều kiện nào có thể khiến bạn đổi quyết định?\n   \n   \n   \n   \nCác chức năng lập luận có thể tái sử dụng ở Speaking Part 3\nFunction\tNatural sentence starter\nState a balanced position\tI can see both sides, but I would lean towards…\nExplain a consequence\tThis could lead to…, particularly when…\nGive an exception\tThat said, the situation may be different for…\nOffer a condition\tIf someone has a strong support network, they may…\n\nMINI-DEBATE   “A person should leave their hometown at least once.” Agree / Disagree / It depends?\n   \n   \n   \n \n04  LISTENING STRATEGY LAB\nINSIGHT → APPLYING EXERCISES  |  Note Completion, MCQ và distractors\nA. Hiểu đúng 2 dạng câu hỏi\nNOTE COMPLETION\tMULTIPLE CHOICE\nCheck the word limit. Predict a noun, verb, adjective or number.\tRead the stem before listening. Underline how the choices differ.\nWrite exactly what you hear, then check grammar/spelling.\tDo not select an option just because its wording is mentioned.\nWatch for numbers, units, percentages and corrections.\tListen for a final decision, correction or contrast.\n\nB. Paraphrase detective – Nối 1–5 với A–E theo nghĩa tương đương\n1. public amenities     2. gather responses     3. remain unchanged     4. weigh up priorities     5. adapt to new surroundings\nA. collect feedback     B. adjust to a new environment     C. community facilities     D. stay stable     E. compare competing needs\n1 ____     2 ____     3 ____     4 ____     5 ____\nC. MCQ – Chỉ chọn thông tin được xác nhận cuối cùng\nSample dialogue (original practice): “At first I considered interviewing 40 people. That seemed too few, so I decided to contact 75.”\nHow many people will the speaker contact?   A. 40    B. 75    C. 115      Answer: ______\nWhy is the first number a distractor? ________________________________________________________________\nD. Mini Form Completion – Giáo viên đọc một lần\nNghe và điền bốn trường thông tin dưới đây. Chú ý chính tả, tên riêng, ngày tháng và đơn vị.\nDate of orientation:  ______________________________________________________________\nContact person (name):  ______________________________________________________________\nIncrease in response rate:  ______________________________________________________________\nHouseholds contacted:  ______________________________________________________________\nE. Checklist trước khi nghe\n□  I read the word limit and answer instructions.\n□  I predict the information type for note gaps.\n□  I compare MCQ options for differences rather than repeated words.\n \n05  LISTENING A  |  RESEARCH PROJECT\nTrao đổi học thuật giữa sinh viên – giảng viên  |  MCQ  |  10 câu\nLISTEN & ANSWER ONLINE  /  Research Project\nhttps://mini-ielts.com/1507/listening/research-project\n \n\nMở link hoặc quét QR để nghe và làm câu hỏi gốc. Worksheet chỉ cung cấp khung ghi đáp án, bằng chứng và chữa lỗi; không sao chép nguyên đề.\nTrước khi nghe – Dự đoán nội dung\nTopic: A student discusses a research investigation with a tutor.\nWhich information might matter?  □ Research purpose   □ Data sources   □ Sample size   □ Questionnaire design\nPredict two expressions the speakers might use:  1. _____________________  2. _____________________\nTrong khi nghe – Điền bảng đáp án\nQuestion\tResponse\tQuestion\tResponse\nQ1\tA / B / C: ______\tQ6\tA / B / C: ______\nQ2\tA / B / C: ______\tQ7\tLetter: ______\nQ3\tA / B / C: ______\tQ8\tLetter: ______\nQ4\tA / B / C: ______\tQ9\tLetter: ______\nQ5\tA / B / C: ______\tQ10\tLetter: ______\n\nQ7–8 form one “choose TWO” set; Q9–10 form another “choose TWO” set. Do not choose the same letter twice within one set.\nSau khi nghe – Phân tích evidence và bẫy đáp án\nQ\tWhat I heard / paraphrase\tWhy another choice was wrong\n1\t\n\n\t\n\n\n3\t\n\n\t\n\n\n6\t\n\n\t\n\n\n9–10\t\n\n\t\n\n\n\nTự đánh giá\nMy raw score: ____ / 10     Hardest item: Q____     Error type:  □ Paraphrase  □ Distractor  □ Number  □ Focus\nOne sentence describing the researcher's final decision: __________________________________________________\n \n06  LISTENING B  |  ORGANIC FARMING\nBài nói học thuật  |  Note Completion + MCQ  |  10 câu\nLISTEN & ANSWER ONLINE  /  Organic Farming\nhttps://mini-ielts.com/1503/listening/organic-farming\n \n\nMở link/quét QR để xem đề và nghe bản gốc. Q1–7: ONE WORD AND/OR A NUMBER; Q8–10: chọn A/B/C. Viết đúng số từ cho phép.\nTrước khi nghe – Dự đoán ý chính\nPossible benefits of organic farming: ________________________________________________________________\nPossible disadvantages or trade-offs: _______________________________________________________________\nBảng ghi đáp án – Dựa trên 10 câu ở website\nNOTE COMPLETION  |  Q1–7\tYOUR ANSWER\tMCQ  |  Q8–10\tYOUR ANSWER\n1\t________________\t8\tA / B / C: _____\n2\t________________\t9\tA / B / C: _____\n3\t________________\t10\tA / B / C: _____\n4\t________________\t\t\n5\t________________\t\t\n6\t________________\t\t\n7\t________________\t\t\n\nPhát hiện bẫy – Ghi lại tín hiệu trong audio\nType\tAn example or phrase I heard\tMy correction\nNumbers / percentages\t\n\t\n\nWord form / spelling\t\n\t\n\nOpinion vs finding\t\n\t\n\n\nPhân tích sâu – Hiểu lập luận, không chỉ tìm đáp án\n1. What trade-off does the speaker present between environmental impact and crop output?\n   \n   \n2. Which claim would you want stronger evidence for? Why?\n   \nMy raw score: ____ / 10.  I lost marks mainly because: _________________________________________________\n \n07  SPEAKING PART 1 + PART 2\nCÂU TRẢ LỜI CÁ NHÂN → BÀI NÓI 2 PHÚT  |  Home and places\nA. Speaking Part 1 – Trả lời trực tiếp, thêm lý do và chi tiết\nFramework: Answer → Because → Example or personal detail  (2–4 natural sentences; do not force a template)\n1. Do you live in a house or an apartment?\n   \n   \n2. What do you like most about your neighbourhood?\n   \n   \n3. Has the place where you live changed in recent years?\n   \n   \n4. Would you prefer to live somewhere else in the future?\n   \n   \nB. Speaking Part 2 – Cue card tự biên soạn\nDESCRIBE A PLACE WHERE YOU FEEL AT HOME\nYou should say: where this place is; when you spend time there; what you usually do there; and explain why you feel connected to it.\n\n1 minute preparation  →  Speak for 1–2 minutes  →  Partner identifies 2 strong details and 1 unclear point.\nWHERE / WHEN\tPEOPLE / ACTIVITIES\tWHY IT MATTERS\n\n\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\n\t\n\n\n\n\n\nMạch kể: Bối cảnh → Một khoảnh khắc → Cảm xúc → Ý nghĩa đối với bản thân.\nExpressions – Chọn cụm phù hợp, không học thuộc cả đoạn\n“One place that immediately comes to mind is…”  •  “I’ve always felt at ease there…”  •  “What makes it special is…”\n“I guess the main reason is…”  •  “If I ever moved away, I would miss…”\nPeer feedback – Góp ý cho bạn học\nOne vivid detail: ______________________________________   One point to improve: ___________________________\n \n08  SPEAKING PART 3 + GRAMMAR\nPHÂN TÍCH → GIẢI THÍCH → CÂN BẰNG QUAN ĐIỂM  |  Part 3 + Grammar\nA. Speaking Part 3 – Chuyển từ chuyện cá nhân sang xã hội\n1.  Why do some people feel disconnected after moving to a large city?\n2.  Should governments invest more in smaller towns to reduce migration?\n3.  Do you think younger generations value personal freedom more than community ties?\n4.  Can digital communities replace the sense of belonging people get locally?\n5.  How might the meaning of “home” change in the future?\nB. Cấu trúc câu trả lời có chiều sâu\nPosition → Reason → Example → Counterpoint → Judgement\nMODEL: “In many cases, moving offers more independence because people can choose where to study or work. For example, a graduate may move to a larger city for specialist training. However, someone without supportive friends could feel isolated. So I think the benefits depend largely on how easily the person can build new relationships.”\nHighlight in the model: opinion / reason / example / counterpoint / conditional conclusion.\nC. Future time conditionals – Ngữ pháp trọng tâm Unit 1\nRULE\nKhi nói về tương lai: If / when / as soon as + PRESENT SIMPLE, mệnh đề chính dùng WILL / MAY / MIGHT + động từ nguyên mẫu. Ví dụ: “If I move abroad, I will try to build a new support network.” Tránh dùng “will” sau “if/when” trong cấu trúc này.\n\nViết lại câu sai, sau đó bổ sung chi tiết để câu tự nhiên hơn.\n1.  If I will move overseas, I will keep in touch with my friends.\n   \n   \n2.  When I will find a new job, I will relocate closer to the office.\n   \n   \n3.  Unless I will feel connected, I will consider moving back.\n   \n   \nD. Vận dụng – Trả lời câu hỏi Part 3 hoàn chỉnh\nQuestion: Is freedom more important than belonging for young adults? Give both sides, one example and your view.\n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n \n09  DETAILED CORRECTION LOG\nLỖI → NGUYÊN NHÂN → SỬA → VẬN DỤNG  |  Học từ lỗi thật\nA. Listening – Ghi lỗi sau khi đối chiếu đáp án và transcript\nSource / Q\tMy answer → Correct\tWhy I was wrong (evidence / trap)\tWhat I will do next time\nResearch Q___\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\nResearch Q___\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\nOrganic Q___\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\nOrganic Q___\t\n\t\n\n\t\n\n\nError codes: P = paraphrase  •  D = distractor  •  N = numbers  •  S = spelling/form  •  A = attention\nB. Speaking – Ghi nhận xét có dẫn chứng, không chấm cảm tính\nAspect\tWhat I said / difficulty\tImproved sentence or next action\nFluency & Coherence\t\n\n\t\n\n\nLexical Resource\t\n\n\t\n\n\nGrammar\t\n\n\t\n\n\nPronunciation\t\n\n\t\n\n\n\nC. Transfer challenge – Biến một lỗi thành quy tắc mới\nChoose one repeated listening trap and one repeated speaking mistake. Explain your fix in English.\nListening: “Next time I hear ______, I will ______.”\n   \n   \nSpeaking: “Instead of saying ______, I can say ______.”\n   \n   \n \n10  HOMEWORK + REFLECTION\nÔN CŨ → GHI ÂM → CHỈNH SỬA  |  Bài tập sau lớp\nA. Homework – 4 nhiệm vụ\n□  HW1  |  Listening – Research Project\nFinish or redo all 10 questions online. Submit score + 3 errors, each with a paraphrase/distractor explanation. Do not consult the solution before attempting.\n□  HW2  |  Listening – Organic Farming\nRedo Q1–10 after class, once without a transcript. Check the word limit and record 3 expressions that signalled an answer or distractor.\n□  HW3  |  Vocabulary retrieval\nWrite 5 original sentences with 3 NEW collocations and 2 REVIEW items. At least 2 sentences should express a trade-off or condition.\n□  HW4  |  Speaking + philosophy\nRecord a 90–120 second response: “Would you sacrifice a sense of belonging for greater personal freedom?” Include a counterargument and one future conditional.\nB. Short reflection – Viết 80–100 từ\n“What does home mean to me, and how might that meaning change in the next ten years?”\n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \n   \nC. Self-assessment – Tự đánh giá dựa trên hành vi cụ thể\nSkill\tNot yet\tSometimes\tConfident\nI can identify why an MCQ option is a distractor.\t□\t□\t□\nI can follow the word limit and spell note answers correctly.\t□\t□\t□\nI can speak for 1–2 minutes using notes, not a script.\t□\t□\t□\nI can express a balanced view with one example.\t□\t□\t□\n\nMY NEXT TARGET:  __________________________________________________________________________________\nSource recordings/questions: mini-ielts.com (Research Project; Organic Farming). All classroom drills, prompts and analysis spaces in this worksheet are newly authored.\n",
